    "original_text": "Exact independently sealed bounded statement:\nFinite real Hilbert/Borel full E including0, actual C2 W, true exp(-W) volume integrability and positive partition, BOTH global mI<=HessW<=MI with0<m<=M.\nGenuine vector id in L2 of normalized tilted Gibbs law. This canonical node keeps the moment premise explicit to rule out totalized covariance outside its integrable domain; the actual paper consumer produces it internally. No covariance/Poincare certificate input.\nFor each direction a, the genuine covariance bilinear form of the normalized BOTH-curvature Gibbs law satisfies Cov_mu(a,a)<=norma^2/m, using the actual linear observable, constant gradient and proven C1 Poincare.\nCanonical BOTH-curvature Gibbs linear covariance upper with genuine vectorL2, actual positive partition and probability normalization; not full anisotropic Brascamp-Lieb. Actual source beta=1 alpha=kappa^-1, 1<=kappa, 0<eta<=1; genuine posterior law R_y, internally produced probability/vectorL2/positive partitions/C2 and normalized-U versus unnormalized-V_eta constant shift. Derive true covariance upper and both Hessian bounds (kappa+eta)^-1 and (1+eta)^-1, then true 1-Lipschitz gradient. Finite real Hilbert/Borel including zero dimension is disclosed representation extension. No input covariance/PI/oracle/moment/normalizer certificate on source Anchor. No joint measurable posterior kernel selector, higher smoothing derivatives, algorithm/Wp/proxy-warmness/main/querycost/composition. PBPS reflected quarter law and source-score remain separate. TV never transfers unbounded expected cost.",
    "text_sha256": "17e5139a9a692330d753b8268c231576c906738ef9a3bc7432eac4cc7c82fd6a"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GibbsLinearCovarianceUpper.gibbs_linear_covariance_upper",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/TechnicalLemmas/FunctionalInequalities/GibbsLinearCovarianceUpper.lean",
    "statement": "{E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E] [CompleteSpace E]\n    (W : E → ℝ) (hW : ContDiff ℝ 2 W)\n    (hI : Integrable (fun x => Real.exp (-W x)))\n    (hZ : 0 < ∫ x, Real.exp (-W x))\n    (m M : ℝ) (hm : 0 < m) (hmM : m ≤ M)\n    (hlower : ∀ x a, m*‖a‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ W) x a a)\n    (hupper : ∀ x a, fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ W) x a a ≤ M*‖a‖^2)\n    (hX : MemLp id 2 ((volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -W x))) :\n    let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -W x)\n    ∀ a : E, ProbabilityTheory.covarianceBilin μ a a ≤ ‖a‖^2/m",
    "statement_sha256": "1028b443c2099d5f3f05946089182c6fbb336733513b987f5f16451632630b17",
    "compiled": true,
    "formalizer": "root-samplinglib-writer",
    "decoder_context": [
      "Measure.tilted mu f = mu.withDensity (fun x => ENNReal.ofReal(exp(f x)/(integral exp(f) dmu))); normalization is totalized if exponential integrability fails. IsProbabilityMeasure nu means nu(univ)=1.",
      "ProbabilityTheory.covarianceBilin mu = ContinuousLinearMap.bilinearComp (covarianceBilinDual mu) (toDualMap R E).toContinuousLinearMap (toDualMap R E).toContinuousLinearMap. With genuine MemLp id2mu and finite probability it equals integral inner(a,x-meanX)*inner(b,x-meanX)dmu. Outside vectorL2 the covariance bilinear is zero, not a covariance estimate.",
      "MemLp id2nu denotes genuine AE strong measurability and finite L2 norm of the position vector. ContDiff R2 denotes actual twice continuously differentiable function, fderiv is genuine Frechet derivative.",
      "gradient f x = (InnerProductSpace.toDual R E).symm(fderiv R f x); true Riesz gradient in the given real Hilbert metric. LipschitzWith1 gradient is the actual global metric inequality.",
      "The conclusion potentials/laws are literal let bodies in the signatures. Finite-dimensional real Hilbert/Borel carrier includes zero dimension, no Nontrivial premise. No nested project-owned estimate-certificate aliases occur in either signature."
    ],
    "compiler_evidence": "Focused3877/standard3; independent statement/source-topology accepted before proof search. Wholemath/blind/source/exact/integration/exposition pending."
